Package: pinnr
Type: Package
Title: Physics-Informed Neural Networks in Native R with 'torch'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Samson", "Obasanmi", email = "obasanmisamson722@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-6935-5479"))
Description: Fits physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) that solve
    ordinary and partial differential equations and estimate unknown
    model parameters from data. Networks are trained by penalising the
    equation residual, boundary and initial conditions, and misfit to
    observations, following Raissi, Perdikaris and Karniadakis (2019)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jcp.2018.10.045>. Everything runs in native R on top of
    'torch', with no 'Python' dependency, and ordinary differential equation
    models written as 'deSolve'-style derivative functions can be used
    directly.
